  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 2.9200000762939453,
      "text": "Welcome to the Cell and Biomolecule data workshop.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 3.5,
      "end": 6.900000095367432,
      "text": "A membrane protein can help transport a substance without making the process",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 6.900000095367432,
      "end": 7.320000171661377,
      "text": "active.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 7.960000038146973,
      "end": 12.079999923706055,
      "text": "In facilitated diffusion, a suitable channel or carrier supports movement down",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 12.079999923706055,
      "end": 15.899999618530273,
      "text": "the relevant gradient without directly coupling transport to an energy source.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 16.8799991607666,
      "end": 20.81999969482422,
      "text": "Active transport moves substances against a gradient by coupling that movement",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 20.81999969482422,
      "end": 22.81999969482422,
      "text": "to energy, directly or indirectly.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 23.399999618530273,
      "end": 27.559999465942383,
      "text": "For an ion, concentration alone is not the whole story: electrical potential",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 27.559999465942383,
      "end": 29.959999084472656,
      "text": "also contributes to the electrochemical gradient.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 30.799999237060547,
      "end": 34.93461388808031,
      "text": "Therefore, a question stating only that a membrane protein is involved does",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 34.93461388808031,
      "end": 35.099998474121094,
      "text": "not",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 35.099998474121094,
      "end": 36.939998626708984,
      "text": "uniquely identify active transport.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 38.2599983215332,
      "end": 41.68000030517578,
      "text": "Read the direction, transported substance and energy coupling before",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 41.68000030517578,
      "end": 42.720001220703125,
      "text": "classifying the mechanism.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 43.05600000000074,
      "end": 47.4960000572212,
      "text": "Suppose a cell membrane permits water but not the solute being compared.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 48.35600019073561,
      "end": 52.47600007629469,
      "text": "If the external solution has a higher effective concentration of that solute,",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 53.11600041961744,
      "end": 54.65600038147047,
      "text": "water tends to leave the cell.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 55.21599984741285,
      "end": 56.65600038147047,
      "text": "An animal cell may shrink.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 57.47600007629469,
      "end": 62.2560007629402,
      "text": "In a hypotonic external solution, net water entry can swell an animal cell,",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 62.896000152588634,
      "end": 66.99600053405837,
      "text": "whereas a plant cell's wall resists expansion and supports turgor.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 67.8559992370613,
      "end": 72.32369168560396,
      "text": "An isotonic condition means no sustained net volume change in the simple",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 72.32369168560396,
      "end": 72.69599938964919,
      "text": "model,",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 73.05600000000075,
      "end": 75.93600106811598,
      "text": "not that individual water molecules stop moving.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 76.81599832153395,
      "end": 81.37599969482497,
      "text": "If the solute can readily cross, its concentration alone may not predict the",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 81.37599969482497,
      "end": 82.73600030517653,
      "text": "long term volume response.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 83.7560007629402,
      "end": 86.83599877929763,
      "text": "State permeability and cell type before choosing a diagram.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 87.16800000000153,
      "end": 91.70287199392227,
      "text": "An organelle question often gives a functional clue rather than a complete",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 91.70287199392227,
      "end": 91.94800020980988,
      "text": "cell",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 91.94800020980988,
      "end": 92.36799980926666,
      "text": "identity.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 93.50800015258942,
      "end": 95.04800011444244,
      "text": "Ribosomes carry out translation.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 95.98799969482575,
      "end": 100.16800000000153,
      "text": "Ribosomes associated with rough endoplasmic reticulum help make many proteins",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 100.16800000000153,
      "end": 104.90799977111969,
      "text": "entering the secretory pathway, and the Golgi apparatus modifies and sorts",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 104.90799977111969,
      "end": 106.08800007629547,
      "text": "material in that pathway.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 107.10800053405914,
      "end": 111.52800061035309,
      "text": "Mitochondria support major stages of aerobic energy metabolism, but finding",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 111.52800061035309,
      "end": 115.52800061035309,
      "text": "many mitochondria does not prove that a cell has no other metabolic pathways.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 115.52800061035309,
      "end": 119.8941543273941,
      "text": "A cell lacking a visible nucleus in one image is not automatically",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 119.8941543273941,
      "end": 120.6880004577652,
      "text": "prokaryotic:",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 121.42799832153473,
      "end": 125.20800091552887,
      "text": "the section, imaging method or cell type may explain the observation.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 126.20800091552887,
      "end": 130.20800091552888,
      "text": "Combine structural evidence with the stated function instead of treating one",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 130.20800091552888,
      "end": 131.98799969482576,
      "text": "image feature as universal proof.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 132.21600000000234,
      "end": 136.23599998092885,
      "text": "An energy diagram shows the same reactants and products with two different",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 136.23599998092885,
      "end": 136.47600022888417,
      "text": "peaks.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 137.3159999046349,
      "end": 141.2959999237084,
      "text": "The lower peak can represent an enzyme catalysed pathway because activation",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 141.2959999237084,
      "end": 142.39600030517812,
      "text": "energy is reduced.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 143.27600041961904,
      "end": 147.05600015259023,
      "text": "The overall free energy difference between the reactants and products remains",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 147.05600015259023,
      "end": 147.55600015259023,
      "text": "the same.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 148.51599923706289,
      "end": 153.09599916076894,
      "text": "Enzymes accelerate approach to equilibrium; they do not, by themselves, change",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 153.09599916076894,
      "end": 157.3083073597467,
      "text": "the equilibrium position or turn every energetically unfavourable reaction",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 157.3083073597467,
      "end": 157.53599969482656,
      "text": "into",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 157.53599969482656,
      "end": 158.33600083923574,
      "text": "a favourable one.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 159.09599916076894,
      "end": 163.40317951652565,
      "text": "Energy coupling can support a cellular process, but coupling is a separate",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 163.40317951652565,
      "end": 163.63600007629628,
      "text": "part",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 163.63600007629628,
      "end": 164.55600015259023,
      "text": "of the explanation.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 165.53599969482656,
      "end": 169.4160007629418,
      "text": "When reading the graph, compare the peak height with the starting level for",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 169.4160007629418,
      "end": 173.85599938965078,
      "text": "activation energy, and compare starting and ending levels for reaction free",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 173.85599938965078,
      "end": 174.19599954223867,
      "text": "energy.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 174.38400000000306,
      "end": 178.54399984741517,
      "text": "A teaching assay reports product concentration rising from two to eight",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 178.54399984741517,
      "end": 181.1440002288849,
      "text": "micromoles per litre over the first three minutes.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 181.74400013351746,
      "end": 186.00399988556214,
      "text": "The average rate in that interval is six divided by three, or two micromoles",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 186.00399988556214,
      "end": 187.0839998092682,
      "text": "per litre per minute.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 187.56400030517884,
      "end": 191.6245119675887,
      "text": "If the early region is approximately linear, this can estimate the initial",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 191.6245119675887,
      "end": 191.8439990844757,
      "text": "rate",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 191.8439990844757,
      "end": 193.304000076297,
      "text": "over that measurement interval.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 194.04399984741517,
      "end": 197.88400000000306,
      "text": "Do not divide the final concentration by time without subtracting the starting",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 197.88400000000306,
      "end": 198.22400015259095,
      "text": "value.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 198.62399977112122,
      "end": 203.304000076297,
      "text": "A later plateau can reflect substrate depletion, product effects or enzyme",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 203.304000076297,
      "end": 207.3439990844757,
      "text": "instability, so an endpoint alone does not give the same information.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 208.48399847412415,
      "end": 212.6839992370636,
      "text": "Compare assays using matching units, observation periods and the same defined",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 212.6839992370636,
      "end": 213.0840007629425,
      "text": "readout.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 213.28800000000365,
      "end": 217.42799986648924,
      "text": "At a fixed enzyme amount and suitable conditions, raising substrate",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 217.42799986648924,
      "end": 221.90799988556273,
      "text": "concentration can increase the initial rate until the enzyme system approaches",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 221.90799988556273,
      "end": 222.50800026703246,
      "text": "saturation.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 223.28800000000365,
      "end": 227.7080000762976,
      "text": "A rate plateau does not mean that catalysis has stopped; it can mean that",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 227.7080000762976,
      "end": 230.00799931335814,
      "text": "adding more substrate produces little further increase.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 230.62800015259154,
      "end": 234.78800000000365,
      "text": "In the simple reversible competitive inhibition model, inhibitor and substrate",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 234.78800000000365,
      "end": 238.90800083923705,
      "text": "compete for access at the active site, and sufficiently high substrate can",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 238.90800083923705,
      "end": 240.6480006103552,
      "text": "reduce the inhibitor's relative effect.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 241.0879992370642,
      "end": 243.5879992370642,
      "text": "Do not apply that conclusion to every inhibitor.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 244.30800045776732,
      "end": 248.18800152588256,
      "text": "A single lowered rate does not uniquely identify an inhibition mechanism.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 249.26799954223998,
      "end": 253.62800015259154,
      "text": "Compare the response across conditions and keep enzyme amount, temperature and",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 253.62800015259154,
      "end": 254.44800000000433,
      "text": "pH controlled before claiming a specific model.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 254.44800000000433,
      "end": 258.68799977112246,
      "text": "Two samples show different enzyme activity at different pH values.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 259.3280001144452,
      "end": 263.29107663257736,
      "text": "The difference can reflect changes in ionisation of important groups,",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 263.29107663257736,
      "end": 263.80799965668155,
      "text": "substrate",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 263.80799965668155,
      "end": 265.6280003051801,
      "text": "binding or structural stability.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 266.36800007629824,
      "end": 270.1280003051801,
      "text": "It does not establish a universal optimum pH for all enzymes.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 270.86800007629824,
      "end": 274.7679996948285,
      "text": "Likewise, warming can initially increase rate, while sufficiently high",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 274.7679996948285,
      "end": 277.9480000000043,
      "text": "temperature can disrupt enzyme structure and reduce activity.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 278.2679996948285,
      "end": 282.4279995422406,
      "text": "A low rate at one temperature does not alone prove permanent denaturation;",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 282.98800091553164,
      "end": 286.8879986267133,
      "text": "additional evidence is needed to distinguish reversible effects from",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 286.8879986267133,
      "end": 287.8679981689496,
      "text": "irreversible damage.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 288.5479984741254,
      "end": 292.9279995422406,
      "text": "When testing temperature, keep other conditions comparable, including pH and",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 292.9279995422406,
      "end": 293.6079998474164,
      "text": "enzyme amount.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 294.6880016784711,
      "end": 297.83723028799636,
      "text": "Describe the measured difference first, then state only the mechanism",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 297.83723028799636,
      "end": 298.24799923706485,
      "text": "supported",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 298.24799923706485,
      "end": 299.7880001525922,
      "text": "by the experimental design.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 300.7680000000052,
      "end": 306.1480001144461,
      "text": "A tissue snapshot contains forty cells visibly in mitosis among five hundred",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 306.1480001144461,
      "end": 306.84799992371126,
      "text": "counted cells.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 307.7280000381522,
      "end": 310.02800022888704,
      "text": "Its mitotic index is eight percent.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 310.02800022888704,
      "end": 314.0479997329764,
      "text": "That is an observed fraction, not automatically eight percent of every",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 314.0479997329764,
      "end": 315.5479997329764,
      "text": "individual cell's cycle time.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 316.7280000381522,
      "end": 320.34799992371126,
      "text": "Estimating stage duration from a snapshot requires assumptions about an",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 320.34799992371126,
      "end": 325.0480006866507,
      "text": "appropriately sampled, asynchronous population, steady behaviour and the",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 325.0480006866507,
      "end": 327.2080005340628,
      "text": "absence of major selection or arrest effects.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 328.02800022888704,
      "end": 332.9279998474173,
      "text": "Interphase is not an inactive waiting period: it includes growth and, during S",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 332.9279998474173,
      "end": 334.3679984741263,
      "text": "phase, DNA replication.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 335.2680000000052,
      "end": 339.72799908447786,
      "text": "If a treatment raises the mitotic index, cells may be entering mitosis faster",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 339.72799908447786,
      "end": 342.6879981689505,
      "text": "or spending longer there, among other possibilities.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 343.1680015258841,
      "end": 346.12800061035676,
      "text": "The fraction alone does not distinguish those mechanisms.",
      "chapter": 7
    }
  ]
}
